  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following relation is not correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>P&#916;V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;S</mi><mi>sys</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#916;S</mi><mi>surr</mi></msub><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T&#916;S</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Enthalpy,&nbsp;in a thermodynamic system, is the measure of its energy which is equal to the sum of the internal energy and the product of its pressure and volume.</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>PV</mi></math> (By definition)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mfenced><mi>PV</mi></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>V&#916;P</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P&#916;V</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;at constant pressure</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>P&#916;V</mi></math>&nbsp;So, option A is incorrect.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>&nbsp;First law of thermodynamics.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;S</mi><mi>sys</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#916;S</mi><mi>surr</mi></msub><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#916;S</mi><mi>Universe</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp; A form of second law of thermodynamics.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T&#916;S</mi></math>&nbsp;Second law of thermodynamics.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>"
  }
}